# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must stay LF on checkout too. A CRLF shebang (`#!/bin/bash\r`)
# breaks the Docker image: the kernel can't find interpreter `/bin/bash\r`, so
# local `docker compose up -d --build` on Windows machines with
# `core.autocrlf=true` fails with `exec /hermeswebui_init.bash: no such file
# or directory`.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Git LFS is intentionally NOT used in this repository.
#
# 2026-07-31: GitHub refuses LFS object uploads to forks of public
# repositories (https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/working-with-files/managing-large-files).
# joshhmann/hermes-webui-hyrax is a public fork of nesquena/hermes-webui, so the
# fork's LFS endpoint rejects every batch upload. The binary assets
# (hyrax-assets/embodiment/*.vrm, hyrax-assets/vn/**, hyrax-assets/essence/frames/**)
# are therefore untracked and served from local disk via the authenticated
# allowlist route (/api/hyrax/assets/*). Text metadata (ASSET_MANIFEST.json,
# SOURCE_SNAPSHOT.json, PROVENANCE.md, frames.registry.json) remains tracked.
